        "problem": "Which set is equivalent to $A={x\\in Q\\,:\\,\\operatorname{sin}\u2061(2\\pi x)=0}?$",
        "worked_solution": "Notice that the solutions to the equation\n\n$$\n\\operatorname{sin}\u2061(2\\pi x)=0\n$$\n\n are given by\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}2\\pi x & =n\\pi  \\\\ 2x & =n \\\\ x & =\\frac{n}{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhere $n\\in Z.$ \n\nSubstituting different values of $n,$ we see that the solutions are\n\n$$\nx=0,\\,\\pm \\frac{1}{2},\\,\\pm 1,\\,\\pm \\frac{3}{2},\\,\u2026\n$$\n\nTherefore, our set $A$ is equivalent to \n\n$$\nA={0,\\,\\pm \\frac{1}{2},\\,\\pm 1,\\,\\pm \\frac{3}{2},\\,\u2026}.\n$$",
